=1,$ and $b=4.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{4}x-\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{1}{4}x-\\frac{1}{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{16}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{16}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+\\frac{16}{{x}^{2}}+8} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{4x}$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{2})|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)+\\frac{1}{8}(4)^{2}]-[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)+\\frac{1}{8}(1)^{2}] \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡4+2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡4+\\frac{15}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536117 true] [17592186384392 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384393 13194139536117 true] [17592186384392 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384394 13194139536117 true] [17592186384392 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384395 13194139536117 true] [17592186384392 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384396 13194139536117 true] [17592186384392 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384397 13194139536117 true] [17592186384392 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536117 true] [17592186384392 1041 "selection" 13194139536117 true] [17592186384392 1104 #edb/ref 17592186384396 13194139536117 true] [17592186384392 1110 #uuid "2e388846-ab83-514e-8fda-927ace8262c8" 13194139536117 true] [17592186384393 1034 "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4" 13194139536117 true] [17592186384393 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536117 true] [17592186384393 1111 #uuid "de481db3-c405